"""
Why the contacts land near the pad tips: MEASUREMENT ONLY (David, Oct 26, step 1). Normal layout, beaker total 0.20 kg, one episode per run.

    MUJOCO_GL=egl python experiments/grip_pad_cause.py [--rotate-deg 7.5] --out data/grip_pad_cause/<name>

At the end of the closing (the first tick of the lift):
  a  the two pads' inner faces from the finger collision meshes (the triangles whose normals face the other finger within 25 degrees): each face's normal against the closing axis (the yaw part about the
     vertical, the pitch part out of the horizontal), the angle between the two faces (0 = parallel), the gap between the faces at the tip end and at the root end;
  b  the beaker's wall segments: how many, the angle of the segment pattern against the closing axis (the facet nearest each finger), the facet's width; where a perfectly round beaker of the same
     radius would touch each pad (the tangent point of the circle on the pad plane, from the axis along the approach axis) against where the contacts really are;
  c  with --rotate-deg X the beaker is turned about its own vertical axis by X degrees at the first tick (harness only), before anything moves; the contacts are measured the same way.
"""

